        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Ribbon or sash of printed silk, satin and velvet, France, 1890-1899"@en , "Silk ribbon, probably intended as a sash, with a white satin ground with a floral design of peony-like flowers in magenta, blue, mauve, black and pale green, set against a slate grey trellis. The pattern is printed on the warp (chiné), and parts of the design are cut by the velours sabré method."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/5d3aa851-e313-394e-830c-fd7fd0bbf108> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Ribbon or sash of printed silk, satin and velvet, France, 1890-1899"@en , "Silk ribbon, probably intended as a sash, with a white satin ground with a floral design of peony-like flowers in magenta, blue, mauve, black and pale green, set against a slate grey trellis. The pattern is printed on the warp (chiné), and parts of the design are cut by the velours sabré method."@en ;
